---
import BlogPostLayout from "../../layouts/BlogPostLayout.astro";
import BlogByline from "../../components/BlogByline.astro";
import Icon from "../../components/Icon.astro";

// Make this page dynamic via SSR
export const prerender = false;

const publishDate = new Date("November 2 2026");
const readTime = "5 min read";

const isPublished = new Date().getTime() >= publishDate.getTime();

---

<BlogPostLayout
  title="Holiday-Ready Kitchen: Deep Clean Guide"
  schemaTitle="Getting Your Kitchen Holiday-Ready: A Deep Clean Guide"
  description={isPublished ? "Get your kitchen holiday-ready with a professional deep clean. Ovens, grout, appliances & more — serving Huntsville, Nashville, Florence & the Shoals area." : "Coming Soon: Getting Your Kitchen Holiday-Ready: A Deep Clean Guide"}
  publishDate={publishDate}
  noindex={!isPublished}
>
  <!-- Hero Section -->
  <section class="pt-24 pb-16 bg-gradient-to-br from-gray-900 via-gray-800 to-gray-900">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
      <div class="text-center">
        <span class="inline-block px-4 py-2 bg-[#FFA985]/20 text-[#FFA985] rounded-full text-sm font-medium mb-6">
          Specialty
        </span>
        <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl lg:text-6xl font-bold text-white mb-6 leading-tight">
          Getting Your Kitchen Holiday-Ready: A Deep Clean Guide
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 mb-8 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
          {isPublished ? "Expert Cleaning Guide" : "Coming November 2 2026."}
        </p>
        <div class="mb-8">
          <BlogByline variant="dark" date={publishDate} readTime={readTime} />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Main Content Toggle based on Published Date -->
  {isPublished ? (
    <article class="py-16 bg-white">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
          <!-- TODO: REPLACE THIS SECTION WITH YOUR ACTUAL BLOG CONTENT -->
          <h2>How Do You Get Your Kitchen Holiday-Ready with a Deep Clean?</h2>
<p><strong>The key to a holiday-ready kitchen is a deep clean that covers every surface and every corner — including the ones you forget about until company is coming. A systematic cleaning routine restores and protects your space.</strong></p>
<p>As the holiday season approaches, your kitchen becomes the hub of festive activities. From family gatherings to holiday feasts, a clean kitchen sets the stage. For residents of The Shoals & Surrounding Areas, here's a step-by-step guide to getting your kitchen holiday-ready with a deep clean.</p>

<h3>Why a Deep Clean is Essential for the Holidays</h3>
<p>During the holidays, your kitchen endures more traffic and usage than usual. A thorough deep clean not only ensures a welcoming environment but also maintains the hygiene standards necessary for food preparation. Investing in a deep clean is a proactive step in preserving the longevity and appearance of your kitchen.</p>

<h3>Step-by-Step Holiday Kitchen Deep Clean Guide</h3>

<h4>1. Declutter and Organize</h4>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Clear Countertops:</strong> Remove non-essential items to create a clean and efficient workspace.</li>
  <li><strong>Organize Cabinets:</strong> Sort through pantry items, discard expired products, and arrange essentials for easy access.</li>
</ul>

<h4>2. Clean Appliances</h4>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Refrigerator:</strong> Empty, clean shelves and drawers with a mixture of warm water and mild detergent. Wipe down the exterior.</li>
  <li><strong>Oven:</strong> Use a baking soda paste to tackle baked-on grease. Wipe clean and finish with a vinegar rinse.</li>
  <li><strong>Dishwasher:</strong> Run an empty cycle with a cup of vinegar to eliminate odors and buildup.</li>
</ul>

<h4>3. Restore Surfaces</h4>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Countertops:</strong> Use a suitable cleaner for your countertop material to remove stains and polish the surface.</li>
  <li><strong>Cabinets and Backsplash:</strong> Wipe down with a damp cloth and mild cleaner, paying attention to handles and edges.</li>
</ul>

<h4>4. Floors and Walls</h4>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Floors:</strong> Sweep and mop, focusing on corners and under appliances where dirt accumulates.</li>
  <li><strong>Walls:</strong> Spot clean with a gentle solution to remove splatters and fingerprints.</li>
</ul>

<h4>5. Final Touches</h4>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Windows:</strong> Clean inside and out for clear, streak-free glass.</li>
  <li><strong>Lighting Fixtures:</strong> Dust and polish to enhance the kitchen's brightness and ambiance.</li>
</ul>

<h3>Why Choose The Valley Clean Team for Your Holiday Kitchen Deep Clean</h3>
<p>For residents of The Shoals & Surrounding Areas, The Valley Clean Team delivers a meticulous kitchen clean with accountability — and if we missed something, tell us within 24 hours and we'll re-clean it at no charge.</p>
<p>Our trained cleaning specialists work a written 44-item checklist every visit, so no detail is overlooked. We restore, maintain, and protect your space, so you can focus on creating holiday memories without the stress of cleaning.</p>

<h3>Rather have us handle it?</h3>
<p>You don't have to carry the holiday cleaning yourself. The Valley Clean Team can take the kitchen off your list — deep cleaning is from $276, with no hidden fees. <strong>Call for your exact price — the number we quote is the number we bill.</strong></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  ) : (
    <article class="py-16 bg-white border-t border-gray-100 shadow-inner">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8 py-12 bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl">
        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none text-center">
          <Icon name="clock" class="w-16 h-16 text-[#FFA985] mx-auto mb-6" />
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-4 mt-0">Article Coming Soon!</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-600 m-0">This article is locked and scheduled to automatically publish on <br/><strong class="text-gray-800 text-xl">November 2 2026</strong>.<br/>Check back then!</p>
          <div class="mt-12">
            <a href="/blog" class="inline-flex items-center justify-center px-6 py-3 text-lg font-semibold text-white bg-[#FFA985] rounded-full hover:bg-[#ff9a70] transition shadow-md no-underline">
              Back to Blog
            </a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </article>
  )}
</BlogPostLayout>
